  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "Terabase assembly collections push k-mer and exact-match queries toward compressed, sublinear-space indexes.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is compressed, sequence-aware indexing applied to large genomic and k-mer collections. Two preprints address k-mer dictionaries built on the SBWT. Batch, Prefetch, Skip, Orient, Squeeze reports a batched, prefetching index with single-orientation storage at 12 bits per canonical k-mer, with streaming 31-mer queries up to 4.9x faster than SSHash. Three further preprints apply compressed-space matching to assemblies and reads. Detection of Maximal Exact Matches uses BWT run-length indexing for SMEMs and MEMs across terabase pangenome assemblies in compressed space and sublinear time. Fast Pangenome Matching Statistics uses move structures for matching statistics and SMEMs, with reported speedups over PHONI and ropebwt3. Genomic tessellations introduces a tessellated BWT index for faster long-read mapping. What is new here is smaller, faster k-mer dictionaries and compressed-space exact-match computation at pangenome scale.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
